; The mode cvars of the stand's profiles (docs/MODES.md section 10, mark integrity S2 of the third review).
; tools/stand/stand_head.py (deploy, and `profile` before every scenario) removes every mode cvar line (coop_split_levels,
; coop_world_server, coop_story_together, coop_soft_host_move, coop_max_map_servers, coop_map_servers_rev,
; coop_mapserver_*) from <stand>\<folder>\user.ltx and writes the lines of the folder's section below instead: the mode a
; stand process runs in comes from HEAD, never from what an earlier run (or a hand) left in the profile. A mark names this
; file's digest (profile_sha256), and this folder is part of the scenario digest: an edit here is an Ядро change.
; Values as the stand ran them on 2026-11-18. appdata_t is the test player's profile; the scenarios copy the host's and
; the single player's profiles from it (New-Profile). appdata_server is the world server's, appdata_ms1 / appdata_ms2
; its map servers'. Step S2 (docs/plans/2026-11-18-two-modes.md, the hybrid removed) took coop_split_levels,
; coop_world_server, coop_story_together and coop_soft_host_move out of the engine: their lines still leave a profile,
; and stand_head.py refuses a row of theirs here (layer guard round 6).
